"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279128044,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-07-27T01:55:53Z","updated_at":"2025-08-02T02:52:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nMaster (0dd9178)\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) / Compatibility ( / Vulkan (Mobile) )- dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 9 7950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen enabling `hdr_2d` the clear color may undergo a color-shift. Notably, this happens with the default `default_clear_color`. Enabling hdr makes the color go from (77, 77, 77) to (76, 76, 76). This might be due to the fact that the default `default_clear_color` is defined with floats (0.3, 0.3, 0.3). This also happens on the Compatiblity renderer where enabling hdr should not have an effect.\n\nWould it be catastrophic to change the default `default_clear_color` from 0.3 grey to 0.302 (`0.30196079611778`) so that the color will remain the same?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nEnable `hdr_2d`.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[hdr_and_woes-of_clear_color.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21450865/hdr_and_woes-of_clear_color.zip)","closed_by":null,"re